{"id": "EUVD-2026-103674", "enisaUuid": "77f97978-41cd-3009-be60-1001d025f234", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nEDAC/altera: Use parent device for devres in altr_portb_setup()\n\nAnchor the devres group and the devm-managed IRQ requests in altr_portb_setup()\nto the actual parent device (device->edac->dev) instead of the embedded struct\ndevice inside the copied per-port altr_edac_device_dev.\n\nThis keeps devres_open_group(), devm_request_irq(), devres_remove_group() and\ndevres_release_group() all referring to the same long-lived device so the\ngroup and the resources allocated inside it are torn down together.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T14:45:24", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:19:31", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8325ecf3f16d764a0e0ba42c95b63f08e38710a8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2cf03ada03532bfb42f06fbf01d9e2a99e6011d7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dc4797c909b6cacb1bb24449e6c57d50a14d73bf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9868f5c077dfe0b606331f2e782484f91a5789a5"], "aliases": ["GHSA-jhg6-q2rv-x659", "CVE-2026-98435"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "02c901e4-450c-3497-a218-ef5f25948b64", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.9"}, {"id": "04c5bced-a1d1-355f-a5a6-f3a1feedc697", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "911049845d7096c27304930ff478cbf3f2623ba3 <9868f5c077dfe0b606331f2e782484f91a5789a5"}, {"id": "1995a594-55d9-3c21-b6c8-69acd7f62b8f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "1aac6563-da8a-3b08-b637-8bdf73530c8e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "1c5a6299-a928-3cca-8ac5-62e1fdff89c1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "911049845d7096c27304930ff478cbf3f2623ba3 <dc4797c